    """The run log's own line style comparison (specs/0026-grouping-and-line-
    styles.md, "Harness runs", --linestyle-sample, P2, with "Planning rulings
    during P2" rulings 1 and 2, and "Planning verification and rulings on P1"
    ruling 2).
    
    Usage: lscmp.py <input archive> <output archive> [--diff <diff.tsv>] [--plant <flag>]
           lscmp.py <input archive> --parts
    
    Reads both archives with zipfile, byte spans and ElementTree, sharing no code
    with the library or the tool; its readers are M3 part 4 P1's gpcmp.py's,
    copied by line range (local, rels_of, workbook_of, w_of, top_level, qname,
    split_name, start_tag, opened, attributes, root_span, is_main, children,
    content_span, rels_prefix_of, bit3, cut, first_insert, et_first, values_of,
    with_attribute, without_attribute, merged, attr_value, col_retagged,
    bare_col, col_span, max_row, rows_of, apply, col_elements, et_cols, et_rows,
    covering). It finds W, the first <sheet> in <sheets> order whose
    relationship type is a worksheet's, and the styles part, the workbook's
    styles relationship's target; M, W's largest row number among its main <c>
    elements (a cell's r, else its row's r), 0 for none; i, the input's cellXfs
    <xf> count (the index add_style returns). From the input it builds the W the
    design gives (specs/0026 "The calls", P2 rulings 1 and 2; specs/0018's row
    creation and <col> split):
    
      row M + 1 carries s="i" then customFormat="1", each replaced between its
      quotes when the row's start tag has it, else appended after the last
      attribute; a present row keeps every other byte (ruling 1); an absent one
      is created as <row r="N" s="i" customFormat="1"/> with the <sheetData>'s
      prefix, before the first row numbered higher, else before </sheetData>;
      column 9 in <cols>: the covering <col> split so the column alone carries
      the edit (min and max replaced in place, the other pieces keeping every
      attribute), style="i" replaced or appended; an uncovered column given
      <col min="9" max="9" style="i"/> with the <cols>' prefix, placed by min;
      the pieces and the created element coalesced as P1 ruling 2 and P1
      verification ruling 2 say (whitespace alone between two pieces dropped
      when they merge), an element the edit did not touch kept as it is; <cols>
      created before the first main root child the 39-name table puts after it
      when W has none.
    
    Of the styles part it checks the spec's three facts, with no design bytes:
    cellXfs one longer, the input's content a byte-identical prefix, its count
    attribute (when present) the new count, the new <xf>'s fontId the input's
    font count; fonts one longer, the input's content a byte-identical prefix,
    its count attribute the new count, the new <font> holding one main <b>;
    every byte outside <fonts> and <cellXfs> the input's.
    
    It compares:
    
      rest_same    W with every main <cols> and <sheetData> cut out is the
                   input's W with its own cut out, byte for byte
      places       W's main root children's names are the input's with a
                   created <cols> where the table puts it
      schema_order W's main root children are in the table's order, one each of
                   <cols> and <sheetData>
      rows_kept    <sheetData> with row M + 1 cut out is the input's with its own
                   row M + 1 cut out, byte for byte
      row_window   the output's row M + 1 is the design's, byte for byte (present
                   edited in place, absent created; ruling 1)
      row_attrs    read with ElementTree, row M + 1 carries exactly the input
                   row's attributes (r alone for one the input lacks) with s and
                   customFormat set, and a created row has no child
      cols_other   the output's <col> elements outside the span the edit covers
                   (column 9 and the input <col> covering it) are the input's
                   outside it, byte for byte, in order
      cols_split   read with ElementTree, the output's <col> elements inside that
                   span cover it exactly, in order; the one over column 9 covers
                   it alone and carries style="i"; every element keeps its
                   source's attributes but min and max (and style on column 9's)
      cols_bytes   the output's <cols> is the design's, byte for byte
      w_bytes      W is exactly the W the design gives
      styles_xfs   cellXfs as above
      styles_fonts fonts as above
      styles_rest  the styles part with <fonts> and <cellXfs> cut out is the
                   input's with its own cut out, byte for byte
      others_same  every entry but W and the styles part is the input's, byte
                   for byte, the names the input's in the input's order
      read_back    read with ElementTree, the tool's figures: row M + 1 carries
                   s="i" and customFormat="1"; one <col> covers column 9, alone,
                   with style="i"; cellXfs one longer
      xml_values   with --diff, the runner's diff.<label>.tsv for the pair: its
                   xml "values" rows are W's and the styles part's alone, W's
                   in_only and out_only the one-sided counts of the input's
                   values against the design's, the styles part's those of the
                   input's against the output's (no design bytes for it), each
                   value keyed as xlsx-diff keys one; without --diff, no
      flagged      with --diff, the diff's entry rows for W and the styles part
                   carry the flag descriptor exactly when the input's local
                   header for each sets general purpose bit 3, and no other row
                   is flagged; without --diff, no
    
    It prints ONE line of counts and yes/no flags and no text, reference, sheet
    name or part name: the line's counts beside the tool's (rows, present rows,
    cols, col_split, kept_cols, xfs), the shapes (case: 1 when no input <col>
    covers column 9, 0 when the covering one is split, 2 when it covers column 9
    alone; created_cols, created_rows, edited_rows). --parts prints W's part
    name and 1, 0 or - for its bit 3, then the styles part's name and its bit 3,
    one per line, for the log to compare with the runner's rows without
    printing them. --plant <flag> changes the output as read so that the named
    flag turns to no; the line then says planted=yes, or planted=no when the
    pair gives the plant nothing to change.
    """
    import collections
    import posixpath
    import re
    import sys
    import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
    import zipfile
    
    MAIN = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/spreadsheetml/main")
    RELS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/relationships"
    ATTR = ("http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships",
            "http://purl.oclc.org/ooxml/officeDocument/relationships")
    
    # ECMA-376 Part 1, 18.3.1.99, the worksheet root's children in order: this
    # program's own copy (specs/0018, "Creating an element"), not the crate's.
    TABLE = (
        "sheetPr dimension sheetViews sheetFormatPr cols sheetData sheetCalcPr "
        "sheetProtection protectedRanges scenarios autoFilter sortState "
        "dataConsolidate customSheetViews mergeCells phoneticPr "
        "conditionalFormatting dataValidations hyperlinks printOptions pageMargins "
        "pageSetup headerFooter rowBreaks colBreaks customProperties cellWatches "
        "ignoredErrors smartTags drawing legacyDrawing legacyDrawingHF drawingHF "
        "picture oleObjects controls webPublishItems tableParts extLst").split()
    assert len(TABLE) == 39
    
    COMMENT = b"<!-- planted -->"
    CELL = re.compile(r"^([A-Z]+)([1-9][0-9]*)$")
    
    class OutOfDesign(Exception):
        """The input is one the write refuses or this comparison does not model."""
    
    
    def local(tag):
        if tag.startswith("{"):
            ns, _, name = tag[1:].partition("}")
            return ns, name
        return "", tag
    
    
    def rels_name(part):
        d, base = posixpath.split(part)
        return posixpath.join(d, "_rels", base + ".rels") if base else "_rels/.rels"
    
    
    def rels_of(z, part):
        """(Id, Type, resolved target or None) of a part's rels."""
        name = rels_name(part)
        if name not in z.namelist():
            return []
        out = []
        for el in ET.fromstring(z.read(name)).iter("{%s}Relationship" % RELS):
            external = el.get("TargetMode") == "External"
            target = el.get("Target", "")
            resolved = None if external else (
                target[1:] if target.startswith("/")
                else posixpath.normpath(posixpath.join(posixpath.dirname(part), target)))
            out.append((el.get("Id"), el.get("Type", ""), resolved))
        return out
    
    
    def workbook_of(z):
        office = [t for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, "") if ty.endswith("/officeDocument")]
        return office[0] if len(office) == 1 else None
    
    
    def w_of(z, workbook):
        """W's part, or None: the first main <sheet> whose relationship is a
        worksheet's."""
        by_id = {i: (ty, t) for (i, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook)}
        for el in ET.fromstring(z.read(workbook)).iter():
            ns, name = local(el.tag)
            if ns in MAIN and name == "sheet":
                rid = next((el.get("{%s}id" % a) for a in ATTR if el.get("{%s}id" % a)), None)
                ty, target = by_id.get(rid, ("", None))
                if ty in (ATTR[0] + "/worksheet", ATTR[1] + "/worksheet"):
                    return target
        return None
    
    
    TOKEN = re.compile(rb"<!--.*?-->|<!\[CDATA\[.*?\]\]>|<[!?][^>]*>|<(/?)[^>]*?(/?)>", re.S)
    
    
    def top_level(data):
        """One (start, end) span per top-level element of some bytes."""
        spans = []
        depth = 0
        at = 0
        for m in TOKEN.finditer(data):
            tok = m.group(0)
            if tok.startswith(b"<!") or tok.startswith(b"<?"):
                continue
            if m.group(1):
                depth -= 1
                if depth == 0:
                    spans.append((at, m.end()))
            elif m.group(2):
                if depth == 0:
                    spans.append((m.start(), m.end()))
            else:
                if depth == 0:
                    at = m.start()
                depth += 1
        return spans
    
    
    def qname(raw):
        return re.match(rb"<([^\s/>]+)", raw).group(1)
    
    
    def split_name(q):
        p, _, n = q.rpartition(b":")
        return (p + b":" if p else b""), n.decode()
    
    
    def start_tag(raw):
        return raw[:raw.find(b">") + 1]
    
    
    def opened(tag):
        slash = tag.rfind(b"/")
        return tag[:slash] + tag[slash + 1:]
    
    
    ATTRS_RE = re.compile(rb'\s([^\s=/>]+)\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')')
    
    
    def attributes(tag):
        """[(name, bytes from the name to the closing quote)] of a start tag, in
        order, namespace declarations among them."""
        return [(m.group(1), tag[m.start(1):m.end()]) for m in ATTRS_RE.finditer(tag)]
    
    
    def attr_matches(tag):
        return list(ATTRS_RE.finditer(tag))
    
    
    def root_span(data):
        """(start of the root's start tag, end of it, start of the root's
        content, end of it, the root's prefix)."""
        m = re.search(rb"<([^\s/>?!]+)", data)
        close = data.find(b">", m.start())
        q = m.group(1)
        if data[close - 1:close] == b"/":
            return m.start(), close + 1, close + 1, close + 1, split_name(q)[0]
        return m.start(), close + 1, close + 1, data.rfind(b"</"), split_name(q)[0]
    
    
    def is_main(raw, parent_prefix, parent_main):
        """Whether an element whose bytes start `raw` is in the main namespace:
        its own declaration of its prefix, else its parent's when the prefix is
        the parent's."""
        p, _ = split_name(qname(raw))
        tag = start_tag(raw)
        decl = rb'\sxmlns:' + re.escape(p[:-1]) if p else rb"\sxmlns"
        own = re.search(decl + rb'\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')', tag)
        if own:
            return own.group(1)[1:-1].decode() in MAIN
        return p == parent_prefix and parent_main
    
    
    def children(data, a, b, rp, parent_main):
        """[(start, end, main local name or None)] of the elements in data[a:b]."""
        out = []
        for (x, y) in top_level(data[a:b]):
            raw = data[a + x:a + y]
            n = split_name(qname(raw))[1]
            out.append((a + x, a + y, n if is_main(raw, rp, parent_main) else None))
        return out
    
    
    def content_span(data, x, y):
        """(start, end) of an element's content, equal for an empty tag."""
        raw = data[x:y]
        tag = start_tag(raw)
        if tag.endswith(b"/>"):
            return x + len(tag), x + len(tag)
        return x + len(tag), x + raw.rfind(b"</")
    
    
    def rels_prefix_of(tag):
        """The prefix a start tag binds to the relationships namespace, or None."""
        for m in re.finditer(rb'\sxmlns:([^\s=/>]+)\s*=\s*("[^"]*"|\'[^\']*\')', tag):
            if m.group(2)[1:-1].decode() in ATTR:
                return m.group(1)
        return None
    
    
    def bit3(zin, name):
        """1 or 0 for whether the input's entry sets general purpose bit 3, -
        when there is no such entry."""
        try:
            return "1" if zin.getinfo(name).flag_bits & 0x08 else "0"
        except KeyError:
            return "-"
    
    
    def cut(data, spans):
        """data with the spans cut out."""
        out, at = [], 0
        for (x, y) in sorted(spans):
            out.append(data[at:x])
            at = y
        out.append(data[at:])
        return b"".join(out)
    
    
    def first_insert(kids, after, root_end):
        """The offset before the first main root child the table puts after the
        position `after`, or the root's end."""
        for (x, _, nm) in kids:
            if nm in TABLE and TABLE.index(nm) > after:
                return x
        return root_end
    
    
    def et_first(root, name):
        for el in root:
            ns, nm = local(el.tag)
            if ns in MAIN and nm == name:
                return el
        return None
    
    
    def values_of(root):
        """The values of an ElementTree as xlsx-diff keys them: each attribute
        (namespace declarations are not attributes here) by element, attribute
        and value; each text node that is not whitespace alone by its element
        and its text (a node's element is the one it stands in: an element's
        text is its own, its tail its parent's)."""
        vals = collections.Counter()
        ws = " \t\n\r"
    
        def walk(el):
            for (k, v) in el.attrib.items():
                vals[("a", el.tag, k, v)] += 1
            if el.text and el.text.strip(ws):
                vals[("t", el.tag, el.text)] += 1
            for c in el:
                walk(c)
                if c.tail and c.tail.strip(ws):
                    vals[("t", el.tag, c.tail)] += 1
    
        walk(root)
        return vals
    
    
    # --- the crate's start-tag edits, written here from their specs (specs/0018
    # "Module package: the calls", specs/0025 "The pass") ---
    
    def name_end(tag):
        return 1 + len(qname(tag))
    
    
    def with_attribute(tag, name, value):
        """`name` set to `value` between its own quotes when present, else
        appended after the last attribute (after the element's name when there
        is none), one space before it."""
        ms = attr_matches(tag)
        for m in ms:
            if m.group(1) == name:
                return tag[:m.start(2) + 1] + value + tag[m.end(2) - 1:]
        at = ms[-1].end() if ms else name_end(tag)
        return tag[:at] + b" " + name + b'="' + value + b'"' + tag[at:]
    
    
    def without_attribute(tag, name):
        """`name` and the whitespace before it removed, the tag as it is when
        `name` is absent."""
        for m in attr_matches(tag):
            if m.group(1) == name:
                frm = m.start(1)
                while frm > 0 and tag[frm - 1:frm] in (b" ", b"\t", b"\n", b"\r"):
                    frm -= 1
                return tag[:frm] + tag[m.end():]
        return tag
    
    
    def merged(tag, sets):
        """A start tag with `sets` first, in their order, and every other
        attribute after them as written, in its order, one space before each;
        empty when it was; the tag as it is with nothing to set."""
        if not sets:
            return tag
        names = [n for (n, _) in sets]
        kept = b"".join(b" " + raw for (n, raw) in attributes(tag) if n not in names)
        head = b"".join(b" " + n + b'="' + v + b'"' for (n, v) in sets)
        return tag[:name_end(tag)] + head + kept + (b"/>" if tag.endswith(b"/>") else b">")
    
    
    def attr_value(tag, name):
        for m in attr_matches(tag):
            if m.group(1) == name:
                return m.group(2)[1:-1]
        return None
    
    
    def col_retagged(tag, mn, mx):
        return with_attribute(with_attribute(tag, b"min", str(mn).encode()), b"max", str(mx).encode())
    
    
    def bare_col(tag):
        return all(n in (b"min", b"max") for (n, _) in attributes(tag))
    
    
    def col_span(tag):
        lo, hi = attr_value(tag, b"min"), attr_value(tag, b"max")
        if lo is None or hi is None or not lo.isdigit() or not hi.isdigit():
            raise OutOfDesign("col")
        lo, hi = int(lo), int(hi)
        if lo == 0 or lo > hi:
            raise OutOfDesign("col")
        return lo, hi
    
    
    def max_row(root):
        m = 0
        for row in root.iter():
            ns, nm = local(row.tag)
            if ns in MAIN and nm == "row":
                for c in row:
                    cns, cnm = local(c.tag)
                    if cns in MAIN and cnm == "c":
                        r = c.get("r")
                        mt = CELL.match(r) if r else None
                        m = max(m, int(mt.group(2)) if mt else int(row.get("r") or 0))
        return m
    
    
    def rows_of(w, s):
        """[(start, end, r as int or None, start tag)] of the main <row> children
        of the first main <sheetData>, and its content span and prefix."""
        x, y = s["el"]["sheetData"][0]
        raw = w[x:y]
        dp = split_name(qname(raw))[0]
        ca, cb = content_span(w, x, y)
        out = []
        for (kx, ky, nm) in children(w, ca, cb, dp, True):
            if nm == "row":
                tag = start_tag(w[kx:ky])
                r = attr_value(tag, b"r")
                out.append((kx, ky, int(r) if r is not None and r.isdigit() else None, tag))
        return out, (ca, cb), dp
    
    
    def apply(data, edits):
        """data with each (start, end, bytes) replacing its span, in order; edits
        at one offset keep their order."""
        out, at = [], 0
        for (a, b, v) in edits:
            out.append(data[at:a])
            out.append(v)
            at = b
        out.append(data[at:])
        return b"".join(out)
    
    
    def col_elements(w, s):
        """[(start, end, min, max, start tag)] of the main <col> children of the
        first main <cols>."""
        if not s["el"]["cols"]:
            return []
        x, y = s["el"]["cols"][0]
        raw = w[x:y]
        cp = split_name(qname(raw))[0]
        ca, cb = content_span(w, x, y)
        out = []
        for (kx, ky, nm) in children(w, ca, cb, cp, True):
            if nm == "col":
                tag = start_tag(w[kx:ky])
                try:
                    mn, mx = col_span(tag)
                except OutOfDesign:
                    mn = mx = -1
                out.append((kx, ky, mn, mx, tag))
        return out
    
    
    def et_cols(root):
        c = et_first(root, "cols")
        if c is None:
            return []
        return [el for el in c if local(el.tag)[0] in MAIN and local(el.tag)[1] == "col"]
    
    
    def et_rows(root):
        d = et_first(root, "sheetData")
        if d is None:
            return []
        return [el for el in d if local(el.tag)[0] in MAIN and local(el.tag)[1] == "row"]
    
    
    def covering(cols, c):
        return next((e for e in cols if e[2] <= c <= e[3]), None)
    
    
    
    
    # --- this phase's design (specs/0026 "The calls", P2 rulings 1 and 2) ---
    
    COLUMN = 9
    FOUR = ("cols", "sheetData")
    FLAGS = ("rest_same", "places", "schema_order", "rows_kept", "row_window", "row_attrs",
             "cols_other", "cols_split", "cols_bytes", "w_bytes", "styles_xfs", "styles_fonts",
             "styles_rest", "others_same", "read_back", "xml_values", "flagged")
    STYLES_TYPES = (ATTR[0] + "/styles", ATTR[1] + "/styles")
    
    
    def styles_of(z, workbook):
        """The styles part's name, or None."""
        for (_, ty, t) in rels_of(z, workbook):
            if ty in STYLES_TYPES:
                return t
        return None
    
    
    def col_styled(tag, i):
        """A covering <col> piece with the style edit: style="i" in place or
        appended."""
        return with_attribute(tag, b"style", str(i).encode())
    
    
    class ColsOut:
        """The coalescing of P1 ruling 2 with P1 verification ruling 2: pieces
        and created elements merged with the one before them when it ends at the
        column before and the two are the same bytes with min and max set aside,
        content too; whitespace alone after a piece waiting is held, dropped when
        the next piece merges into it and written after it otherwise; anything
        else ends a merge."""
    
        def __init__(self):
            self.out = []
            self.open = None
            self.gap = b""
    
        def flush(self):
            if self.open is not None:
                tag, rest, mn, mx, widened = self.open
                self.out.append(col_retagged(tag, mn, mx) if widened else tag)
                self.out.append(rest)
                self.open = None
            self.out.append(self.gap)
            self.gap = b""
    
        def between(self, raw):
            if self.open is not None and raw.strip(b" \t\r\n") == b"":
                self.gap += raw
                return
            self.kept(raw)
    
        def kept(self, raw):
            self.flush()
            self.out.append(raw)
    
        def made(self, tag, rest, mn, mx):
            o = self.open
            if (o is not None and o[3] + 1 == mn and o[1] == rest
                    and col_retagged(o[0], 1, 1) == col_retagged(tag, 1, 1)):
                self.open = (o[0], o[1], o[2], mx, True)
                self.gap = b""
                return
            self.flush()
            self.open = (tag, rest, mn, mx, False)
    
        def finish(self):
            self.flush()
            return b"".join(self.out)
    
    
    def cols_content(data, ca, cb, cp, i):
        """The children of a <cols> (data[ca:cb], prefix cp) with the style edit
        on column 9, coalesced."""
        out = ColsOut()
        done = False
        last_max = 0
        at = ca
        for (x, y, nm) in children(data, ca, cb, cp, True):
            if x > at:
                out.between(data[at:x])
            at = y
            raw = data[x:y]
            if nm != "col":
                out.kept(raw)
                continue
            start = start_tag(raw)
            rest = raw[len(start):]
            mn, mx = col_span(start)
            if mn <= last_max:
                raise OutOfDesign("cols order")
            last_max = mx
            if not done and COLUMN < mn:
                out.made(col_styled(col_retagged(b"<" + cp + b"col/>", COLUMN, COLUMN), i), b"", COLUMN, COLUMN)
                done = True
            if not done and mn <= COLUMN <= mx:
                if COLUMN > mn:
                    out.made(col_retagged(start, mn, COLUMN - 1), rest, mn, COLUMN - 1)
                out.made(col_styled(col_retagged(start, COLUMN, COLUMN), i), rest, COLUMN, COLUMN)
                if COLUMN < mx:
                    out.made(col_retagged(start, COLUMN + 1, mx), rest, COLUMN + 1, mx)
                done = True
                continue
            out.kept(start)
            out.kept(rest)
        if cb > at:
            out.between(data[at:cb])
        if not done:
            out.made(col_styled(col_retagged(b"<" + cp + b"col/>", COLUMN, COLUMN), i), b"", COLUMN, COLUMN)
        return out.finish()
    
    
    def shape(w, root_ns):
        """W's root spans and prefix, its root children, and the spans of <cols>
        and <sheetData>."""
        ts, te, a, b, rp = root_span(w)
        kids = children(w, a, b, rp, root_ns in MAIN)
        return {"ts": ts, "te": te, "a": a, "b": b, "rp": rp, "kids": kids,
                "el": {n: [(x, y) for (x, y, nm) in kids if nm == n] for n in FOUR}}
    
    
    def row_sets(i):
        return ((b"s", str(i).encode()), (b"customFormat", b"1"))
    
    
    def design(win, s, m, i):
        """The W the design gives, its row M + 1's bytes and its <cols>' bytes;
        OutOfDesign when the write would refuse the input."""
        for n in FOUR:
            if len(s["el"][n]) > 1:
                raise OutOfDesign(n)
        if not s["el"]["sheetData"]:
            raise OutOfDesign("sheetData")
        rp = s["rp"]
        edits = []
        if s["el"]["cols"]:
            x, y = s["el"]["cols"][0]
            raw = win[x:y]
            tag = start_tag(raw)
            cp = split_name(qname(raw))[0]
            ca, cb = content_span(win, x, y)
            content = cols_content(win, ca, cb, cp, i)
            cols_el = (opened(tag) if tag.endswith(b"/>") else tag) + content + b"</" + qname(tag) + b">"
            edits.append((x, y, 0, cols_el))
        else:
            at = first_insert(s["kids"], TABLE.index("cols"), s["b"])
            cols_el = b"<" + rp + b"cols>" + cols_content(b"", 0, 0, rp, i) + b"</" + rp + b"cols>"
            edits.append((at, at, 0, cols_el))
        rows, (ca, cb), dp = rows_of(win, s)
        n = m + 1
        present = [(kx, ky, tag) for (kx, ky, r, tag) in rows if r == n]
        if present:
            kx, ky, tag = present[0]
            new = tag
            for (k, v) in row_sets(i):
                new = with_attribute(new, k, v)
            body = new + win[kx + len(tag):ky]
            row_edits = [(kx, kx + len(tag), new)]
        else:
            body = b"<" + dp + b'row r="' + str(n).encode() + b'"'
            for (k, v) in row_sets(i):
                body += b" " + k + b'="' + v + b'"'
            body += b"/>"
            after = next((kx for (kx, _, r, _) in rows if r is not None and r > n), cb)
            row_edits = [(after, after, body)]
        x, y = s["el"]["sheetData"][0]
        tag = start_tag(win[x:y])
        data = win[x:y]
        if tag.endswith(b"/>"):
            data = opened(tag) + b"</" + qname(tag) + b">"
            cb2 = len(opened(tag))
            row_edits = [(cb2, cb2, b) for (_, _, b) in row_edits]
        else:
            row_edits = [(a - x, b - x, v) for (a, b, v) in row_edits]
        edits.append((x, y, 1, apply(data, row_edits)))
        return apply(win, [(a, b, v) for (a, b, _, v) in sorted(edits, key=lambda e: (e[0], e[2]))]), body, cols_el
    
    
    def root_child(data, name):
        """(start, end, content start, content end) of the first main root child
        `name` of a part, or None."""
        m = re.search(rb"<([^\s/>?!]+)", data)
        ts, te, a, b, rp = root_span(data)
        root_main = is_main(data[m.start():te], b"", False)
        for (x, y, nm) in children(data, a, b, rp, root_main):
            if nm == name:
                ca, cb = content_span(data, x, y)
                return x, y, ca, cb
        return None
    
    
    def main_kids(el, name):
        return [c for c in el if local(c.tag)[0] in MAIN and local(c.tag)[1] == name]
    
    
    VALUE_NS = MAIN
    
    
    def plant(flag, wout, sout, others, st):
        """(wout, sout, others) changed so that `flag` turns to no, or None when
        the pair gives the plant nothing to change."""
        s = shape(wout, st["root_ns"])
        o = dict(others)
        if any(len(s["el"][n]) != 1 for n in FOUR):
            return None
        m = st["m"]
    
        def tagged(data, at, tag, new):
            return data[:at] + new + data[at + len(tag):]
    
        def extra(tag):
            return tag[:-2] + b' planted="1"/>' if tag.endswith(b"/>") else tag[:-1] + b' planted="1">'
    
        if flag == "rest_same":
            return wout[:s["te"]] + COMMENT + wout[s["te"]:], sout, o
        if flag == "places":
            other = [(x, y) for (x, y, nm) in s["kids"] if nm not in (None,) + FOUR]
            if not other:
                return None
            x, y = other[0]
            return wout[:y] + wout[x:y] + wout[y:], sout, o
        if flag == "schema_order":
            x, y = s["el"]["cols"][0]
            el = wout[x:y]
            rest = wout[:x] + wout[y:]
            end = rest.rfind(b"</")
            return rest[:end] + el + rest[end:], sout, o
        rows, (ca, cb), _ = rows_of(wout, s)
        if flag == "rows_kept":
            return wout[:ca] + COMMENT + wout[ca:], sout, o
        if flag in ("row_window", "row_attrs"):
            hit = next(((kx, tag) for (kx, _, r, tag) in rows if r == m + 1), None)
            if hit is None:
                return None
            kx, tag = hit
            new = extra(tag) if flag == "row_window" else with_attribute(tag, b"customFormat", b"0")
            return tagged(wout, kx, tag, new), sout, o
        cols = col_elements(wout, s)
        if flag == "cols_other":
            lo, hi = st["span"]
            hit = next(((kx, tag) for (kx, _, mn, mx, tag) in cols if mx < lo or mn > hi), None)
            if hit is None:
                return None
            kx, tag = hit
            return tagged(wout, kx, tag, extra(tag)), sout, o
        if flag == "cols_split":
            hit = next(((kx, tag) for (kx, _, mn, mx, tag) in cols if mn <= COLUMN <= mx), None)
            if hit is None:
                return None
            kx, tag = hit
            return tagged(wout, kx, tag, with_attribute(tag, b"style", b"0")), sout, o
        if flag == "cols_bytes":
            x, y = s["el"]["cols"][0]
            ca2, _ = content_span(wout, x, y)
            return wout[:ca2] + COMMENT + wout[ca2:], sout, o
        if flag == "w_bytes":
            return wout + b"\n", sout, o
        if flag in ("styles_xfs", "styles_fonts"):
            el = root_child(sout, "cellXfs" if flag == "styles_xfs" else "fonts")
            if el is None:
                return None
            x, y, ca2, cb2 = el
            # The last child goes: one fewer than the design gives.
            kids = top_level(sout[ca2:cb2])
            if not kids:
                return None
            kx, ky = kids[-1]
            return wout, sout[:ca2 + kx] + sout[ca2 + ky:], o
        if flag == "styles_rest":
            ts, te, _, _, _ = root_span(sout)
            return wout, sout[:te] + COMMENT + sout[te:], o
        if flag == "others_same":
            name = next(iter(o), None)
            if name is None:
                return None
            o[name] = o[name] + COMMENT
            return wout, sout, o
        if flag == "read_back":
            hit = next(((kx, tag) for (kx, _, r, tag) in rows if r == m + 1), None)
            if hit is None:
                return None
            kx, tag = hit
            return tagged(wout, kx, tag, with_attribute(tag, b"s", b"0")), sout, o
        if flag in ("xml_values", "flagged"):
            return wout, sout, o
        raise KeyError(flag)
    
    
    def yn(v):
        return "yes" if v else "no"
    
    
    def main():
        args = sys.argv[1:]
        zin = zipfile.ZipFile(args[0])
        wb = workbook_of(zin)
        if wb is None or wb not in zin.namelist():
            print("error=no-workbook")
            return
        part = w_of(zin, wb)
        if part is None or part not in zin.namelist():
            print("error=no-worksheet")
            return
        sty = styles_of(zin, wb)
        if sty is None or sty not in zin.namelist():
            print("error=no-styles")
            return
        if args[1:] == ["--parts"]:
            print(part)
            print(bit3(zin, part))
            print(sty)
            print(bit3(zin, sty))
            return
        names_in_order = zin.namelist()
        win = zin.read(part)
        sin = zin.read(sty)
        root_i = ET.fromstring(win)
        sroot_i = ET.fromstring(sin)
        root_ns = local(root_i.tag)[0]
        zout = zipfile.ZipFile(args[1])
        rest = args[2:]
        diff_path = flag_plant = None
        while rest:
            if rest[0] == "--diff" and len(rest) >= 2:
                diff_path, rest = rest[1], rest[2:]
            elif rest[0] == "--plant" and len(rest) >= 2:
                flag_plant, rest = rest[1], rest[2:]
                if flag_plant not in FLAGS:
                    print("error=unknown-plant")
                    return
            else:
                print("error=usage")
                return
        out_names = zout.namelist()
        wout = zout.read(part) if part in out_names else b""
        sout = zout.read(sty) if sty in out_names else b""
        others = {nm: zout.read(nm) for nm in out_names if nm not in (part, sty)}
    
        xfs_in_el = et_first(sroot_i, "cellXfs")
        fonts_in_el = et_first(sroot_i, "fonts")
        if xfs_in_el is None or fonts_in_el is None:
            print("error=out-of-design")
            return
        xfs_in = len(main_kids(xfs_in_el, "xf"))
        fonts_in = len(main_kids(fonts_in_el, "font"))
        i = xfs_in
        m = max_row(root_i)
        s_in = shape(win, root_ns)
        try:
            want, want_row, want_cols = design(win, s_in, m, i)
        except OutOfDesign:
            print("error=out-of-design")
            return
        cols_in = col_elements(win, s_in)
        cov = covering(cols_in, COLUMN)
        span_lo, span_hi = (cov[2], cov[3]) if cov else (COLUMN, COLUMN)
        st = {"root_ns": root_ns, "m": m, "span": (span_lo, span_hi)}
        planted = False
        if flag_plant is not None:
            changed = plant(flag_plant, wout, sout, others, st)
            if changed is not None:
